        "Steve Jobs' experience at Reed College with calligraphy influenced the typography of the Macintosh, as he learned about serif and sans serif typefaces, varying the amount of space between different letter combinations, and what makes great typography great.",
        "This knowledge was later reflected in the Macintosh, which had multiple typefaces and proportionally spaced fonts. “If I had never dropped in on that single course in college, the Mac would have never had multiple typefaces or proportionally spaced fonts."
